The official check resolves the key tax ambiguity: for an end-customer jewellery sale, CBIC says 3% applies to the total transaction value even when making charges are shown separately. The 5% rate concerns registered job-work charges upstream, not a second retail GST charge on making charges. I’m carrying that distinction into the article and calculations.
